[1] Law of Ukraine on Employment of the Population (unofficial ILO translation) — Article 16. Implementation of state policy in the sphere of population employment (версія draft, чинна)
1. The state ensures the implementation of the policy in the sphere of population employment by:

1) implementation of tax, credit and monetary, investment, budget, social, foreign economic and innovation policies with the aim of expanding the scope of employment, ensuring full, productive, freely chosen employment, improving the level of qualification and competitiveness of the workforce;

2) determination of indicators of labor market development and population employment in national programs of economic and social development, programs of economic and social development of the Autonomous Republic of Crimea, regions, districts, cities and their evaluation based on the results of the implementation of such programs;

3) inclusion in the labor market regulation system of measures to introduce incentives for employers to create new jobs; __

4) promotion of increasing the competitiveness of the labor force and employment of the population;

5) social protection of citizens in case of unemployment;

6) promotion of self-employment of the population by stimulating the opening of one's own business, including in rural settlements and depressed areas;

7) development of rural agrarian tourism, clusters of folk crafts;

8) creation of conditions to ensure increased competitiveness of the workforce and its mobility;

9) forecasting and assessment of the impact of employment policies on the labor market;

10) maintaining a list of business entities that provide mediation services in employment abroad. __ Article 17. Bodies ensuring the formation and implementation of state policy in the sphere of public employment

1. The formation and implementation of state policy in the field of population employment is ensured within the limits of their powers by the Verkhovna Rada of Ukraine, the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine, the central body of executive power that ensures the formation of state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration, other central bodies of executive power, the Verkhovna Rada of the Autonomous Republic of Crimea and the Council of Ministers of the Autonomous Republic of Crimea, local state administrations, local self-government bodies.

__

[2] Labour Code of Ukraine (official English translation) — Chapter V REST TIME > Article 71. Prohibition of work on weekend. Exceptional procedure for such work (версія current, чинна)
Uninterrupted weekly rest period must be at least forty-two hours.

### Article 71. Prohibition of work on weekend. Exceptional procedure for such work

Work on weekend is prohibited. Involvement of individual employees to work on these days is only permitted by the elected body of the primary trade union organisation (trade union representative) of the enterprise, institution, organisation and only in exceptional cases specified by law and in Part 2 of this Article.

Involvement of individual employees to work on weekend is allowed in the following exceptional cases:

1) to prevent or eliminate the consequences of natural disasters, epidemics, epizootics, industrial accidents, and the immediate elimination of their consequences;

2) to prevent accidents that endanger or may endanger the life or normal living conditions of people or cause loss or damage to property;

3) to perform urgent, unforeseen work whose immediate performance further determines the normal operation of the entire enterprise, institution, organisation or their individual units;

4) to perform urgent handling operations to prevent or eliminate the downtime of rolling stock or accumulation of goods at points of departure and destination.

The involvement of employees to work on the weekend is carried out under a written order of the owner or their authorised body.

[3] Law of Ukraine on Employment of the Population (unofficial ILO translation) — Article 22. Tasks and functions of the central body of executive power implementing state policy in the sphere of population employment and labor migration, its territorial bodies (версія draft, чинна)
2) ensure the functioning of the Unified Information and Analytical System, in particular, form a database of vacant jobs (positions) on the basis of information received from employers, business entities that provide employment mediation services, from other sources (in particular, from job search information resources);

__

3) keep records of persons applying for employment assistance and the services provided to them;

4) carry out registration of the unemployed, keep records of the services provided to them;

5) organize professional training of the registered unemployed taking into account the current and future needs of the labor market;

6) organize the assignment/confirmation of professional and partial professional qualifications, recognition of the results of informal and informal training for the registered unemployed;

__

7) inform the population, executive authorities and educational institutions about the demand and supply of labor on the labor market, rights and guarantees in the field of employment of the population and in the event of unemployment;

8) collect, process, submit and distribute administrative data on the demand and supply of labor on the labor market, provide social services to the population and employers in accordance with the procedure established by law;

9) analyze indicators of demand and supply of labor force and submit proposals for forecasting the development of the labor market to the central body of executive power, which ensures the formation of state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration;

__

10) participate in the development of the main directions of the implementation of state policy in the field of population employment for the medium-term period, territorial programs of population employment and their implementation;

11) promote the employment of the unemployed at enterprises involved in the implementation of state target programs and infrastructure projects, in accordance with the procedure established by the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine;

12) interact with employers on issues of determining the current and future need for labor force, professional training of the population and staffing of vacant jobs;

13) maintain a list of business entities that provide employment mediation services;

[4] Labour Code of Ukraine (official English translation) — Chapter X LABOUR DISCIPLINE > Article 144. The procedure for applying incentives (версія current, чинна)
Employees of enterprises, institutions, organisations may be subject to any incentives contained in the internal labour regulation rules approved by personnel.

### Article 144. The procedure for applying incentives

Incentives are applied by the owner or their authorised body together or in agreement with the elected body of the primary trade union organisation (trade union representative) of the enterprise, institution, organisation.

Incentives are announced by order in a solemn ceremony and are entered in the employment records of employees according to the rules of their maintenance.

[5] Labour Code of Ukraine (official English translation) — Section I GENERAL PROVISIONS > Article 9-1. Additional, in comparison with the legislation, labour and social benefits (версія current, чинна)
Enterprises, institutions, organisations within the limits of their powers and at their own expense can establish additional, in comparison with the legislation, labour and social benefits for employees.

The enterprise may financially reward employees of medical, children's, cultural and educational, educational and sports institutions, catering organisations and organisations that serve the labour collective and are not part of it.

[6] Law of Ukraine on Employment of the Population (unofficial ILO translation) — Article 15. Principles and purpose, main directions of state policy in the sphere of population employment (версія draft, чинна)
6) assistance to enterprises, institutions and organizations regardless of the form of ownership, type of activity and management in the professional development of employees;

7) balancing supply and demand regarding the volume and level of qualification of the labor force on the labor market through systematic forecasting of the needs of the economy;

- 8) promotion of employment of citizens;

9) ensuring the creation of equal opportunities for economic entities to implement infrastructure projects and targeted programs financed by state funds;

10) coordination and control of the activities of business entities that provide employment mediation services;

11) returning the unemployed to productive employment;

12) international cooperation in the sphere of ensuring social protection of Ukrainian citizens working abroad;

13) interaction of executive authorities, local self-government bodies, employers and trade unions with the aim of ensuring full and productive freely chosen employment, in particular implementation of measures to promote employment of the population;

14) ensuring effective and targeted use of funds aimed at the implementation of state policy in the field of population employment;

15) implementation of measures promoting the employment of citizens who are not sufficiently competitive on the labor market ( part one of Article 14 of this Law);

16) encouragement of employers who maintain existing and create new jobs primarily for citizens who are not sufficiently competitive on the labor market (part one of Article 14 of this Law);

17) ensuring the cooperation of the central executive body that implements state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration, business entities that provide employment mediation services, other employment mediators and institutions for social, professional and labor rehabilitation of persons with disabilities, social service centers for youth;

18) protection of the domestic labor market by regulating the employment of foreign workers.

[7] Law of Ukraine on Employment of the Population (unofficial ILO translation) — Article 24. Social services and measures to promote employment of the population (версія draft, чинна)
1. The list (types) of social services in the field of employment is determined by this Law and Article 7 of the Law of Ukraine "On Mandatory State Social Insurance in Case of Unemployment" and includes:

- 1) information services;

2) consulting services;

- 3) professional orientation;

- 4) professional training;

5) individual employment planning;

- 6) services for employers;

- 7) employment services;

8) other services related to employment provided for by the procedure for providing social services to subjects of the labor market in the field of employment.

Social services to the subjects of the labor market are provided by career counselors, specialized career counselors, consultants on work with employers in accordance with the procedure determined by the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine.

2. Measures to promote employment of the population include:

1) professional orientation and professional training;

2) stimulating the creation of new jobs, employment of the unemployed;

3) promotion of self-employment of the population, organization of business activities;

4) assistance in providing young people with their first job, internship with an employer;

5) promoting the employment of persons who are unable to compete on equal terms in the labor market;

6) ensuring the participation of the unemployed in public works and other works of a temporary nature;

7) other programs to promote employment of the population, which are introduced by separate decisions of the Cabinet of Ministers of Ukraine.

3. Individual employment planning consists in determining the list and sequence of providing social services in the field of employment, involvement in measures to promote employment of the population on the labor market, to which the registered unemployed person is entitled, taking into

account the results of his profiling, which is reflected in the individual employment plan.

Profiling is carried out in accordance with the methodology approved by the central executive body, which ensures the formation of state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration.

An exemplary form, procedure for drawing up and maintaining an individual employment plan for a registered unemployed person is approved by the central executive body, which ensures the formation of state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration.

